course: dictionary
lesson: 2268
title: Creativity: making something new
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Creativity is the ability to make new things or think of new and original ideas. It is a noun, and it is uncountable: you do not say "a creativity", you say "show creativity" or "full of creativity".
explain: Creativity is used in art, music, writing and drama, and also in maths and science when you solve a problem in a new way. «Boredom is often the start of creativity» means that when nothing much is happening, your mind may start to make something new.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. «On a rainy afternoon a boy in Manchester turned a sofa and two blankets into a castle» shows creativity, because he used ordinary things in a new way. You can use your creativity too: a box, a blanket or a cardboard tube can become something new.
fact: Creativity is the ability to make new things or think of new and original ideas.
fact: Creativity is uncountable: you can show creativity, use your creativity or be full of creativity.
fact: «Boredom is often the start of creativity» means boredom can lead to new ideas.
fact: Creativity is used in art, music, writing, drama, design and technology, and also in maths and science.
fact: «Creative» is the adjective: a creative idea is a new and original one.
exercise: «Boredom is often the start of creativity.» What is creativity? | Being very tired after a long day | *The ability to make new things or think of new ideas | Cleaning up a messy room | A type of screen game
exercise: «On a rainy afternoon a boy in Manchester turned a sofa and two blankets into a castle.» What did the boy show? | Laziness, because he did nothing | Sadness about the rain | Hunger | *Creativity, by using ordinary things in a new way
exercise: Which phrase uses creativity correctly? | creativities are hard | *show creativity | a creativity | many creativities
test: «When you are bored with no screen, you can build a den, read, draw or write a story.» Which of these is an example of creativity? | Sitting still and doing nothing at all | Watching the clock until bedtime | *Building a den from cushions and blankets | Turning off all the lights
test: Mia's teacher says, «Mia is full of creativity!» What does she mean? | *Mia has lots of new and original ideas | Mia has lost her pencil | Mia is very tired | Mia must sit at the back
exam: Ella says creativity is something you can count, like three apples. Who is right? | Both are wrong, because creativity is a sport | *Ella is wrong, because creativity is uncountable and has no plural | Ella is right, and there are three creativities in her bag | Ella is right, because creativity is like apples
